ly  ! Avoid adverbs when possible.
 are   Often begins a passive construction
 as a consequence = thus
 as a result  = thus
 for many
 for the purpose of
 furthermore
 in which you can = to
 it is easy to = you can
 it is possible to  = you can
 it is much more  Wordy construct
 is Often begins a passive construction
 it should allow  {subject} should
 kinds of
 nonetheless  = still
 not so when  = when
 one of the = a
 prior to = before
 rather than to  Use "instead of"
 seem to
 so easy  = easy
 so that  = that
 than meets the eye Cliche'd phrase
 will Use present tense; for example, "will display" -> "displays"
